{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And you shall be altogether joyful.</b> You find written three joys regarding the festival of Sukkot: ושמחת בחגך, אך שמח, and ושמחת לפני ה' אלהיך, which is written in the section of אמור אל הכהנים. And regarding Shavuot, only one is written: ושמחת לפני ה' אלהיך. And regarding Pesach, no joy is written at all, because on Pesach the grain has not yet been gathered, nor the fruits of the tree. And on the festival of Shavuot the grain has already been gathered, so there is one joy and no more, for the fruits of the tree have not yet been gathered, and also the grain has not [been brought] into the house. But on the festival of Sukkot, when the grain and the fruits of the tree have been gathered and also everything has been collected into the house — then the joy is complete; therefore three joys are written concerning it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:02.240107168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}